     and to modify them, so long as the result stays an Agent-Authored
     Derived Work.

4.2  Every copy of the Work or of an Agent-Authored Derived Work that
     You Distribute must
       (a) include this license unchanged, adding it if the copy You
           received lacked it, and keep every notice and agent-authored
           statement the copy carries;
       (b) if You changed it, state in plain text, where a recipient
           reading the copy will see it, that Your changes are
           agent-authored, and name the Agents that made them: the model
           where You know it, otherwise the product. Where a change is a
           removal under Section 1.5(b), or was made by software that
           only transforms content (Section 1.2), say so instead. A copy
           You Distribute unchanged need only keep the statements it
           carries.
     This license gives no right to use any Agent provider's name or
     logo; their own terms govern that. You may add, in a separate
     notice and not in this license text, a disclaimer or limit of Your
     own liability, or a warranty, support or indemnity You offer on
     Your own account. Such a notice speaks for You alone and does not
     restrict what this license permits.

4.3  You may Distribute an Agent-Authored Derived Work under terms of
     Your choice. The parts of the Work it contains stay under this
     license, or a later version of it the Licensor publishes, at Your
     choice. Terms You add do not limit what this license permits for
     those parts. Files that carry another license keep it.

4.4  If the Licensor asks You in writing how a change You made in an
     Agent-Authored Derived Work You have Distributed was produced, You
     must say within 30 days which Agent made it or, if none did, how it
     was made. If You still have the prompts or transcript, You must
