4.5  You may rely on a statement under 4.2(b) that a copy carries. If it
     is untrue and You had no reason to think so, Distributing that copy
     is permitted under Section 3 until the Licensor tells You it is
     untrue.

5. HUMAN-AUTHORED DERIVED WORKS

5.1  You may make a Human-Authored Derived Work only if You are a
     natural person, and only from Human-Authored Content You composed
     yourself. You may copy and run it only for Your own use, on devices
     You control. No one else may use it, including an employer, client
     or company You work for. Running it as a tool in Your own work,
     including work You do for others, is Your own use, not a product or
     service under 5.2; what it produces when run is not a Derived Work
     (Section 3). Content composed independently of the Work may be
     combined with it under its own terms (Section 1.6). Holding a copy
     where Section 1.10 allows, and supplying it to an Agent as input,
     are within this permission.

5.2  You may not Distribute it, sublicense it, sell it, let anyone else
     use it, or offer it or its functions to anyone else as a product or
     service, paid or unpaid, including by network access. Giving anyone
     else Human-Authored Content composed to change the Work or a
     Derived Work, so that they can make a Human-Authored Derived Work
     from it, is Distributing one. Making, copying or running it for any
     other purpose is outside the permission in 5.1.

5.3  Having an Agent repeat the Human-Authored Content of a
     Human-Authored Derived Work, or keep its wording or order with only
     small changes, does not make the result an Agent-Authored Derived
     Work (Section 1.5).

5.4  Apart from Section 7, the only exception to 5.2 is sending the
     Human-Authored Derived Work privately to the Licensor under
     Section 6. Any other use requires a separate written license from
     the Licensor.

6. SUBMISSIONS

You may submit Agent Output, Agent-Authored Derived Works, bug reports
and descriptions of changes to the Licensor through the channel the
Work's README names. The Licensor does not include Human-Authored
Content in the Work. You may send a Human-Authored Derived Work
privately to the Licensor to show a problem or a wanted behaviour; the
Licensor treats it as a report and does not include it.

By submitting content for inclusion You grant the Licensor a perpetual,
irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free license to use, modify, Distribute
and sublicense it under this license, any later version the Licensor
publishes, or other terms, and You warrant that You hold the rights in
it, or that whoever holds them, for example Your employer or the holder
of the account the Agent ran under, has permitted You to submit it.
Rights the law does not let You waive are unaffected.

Publishing a Human-Authored Derived Work, including in a public fork or
pull request, is Distribution, not submission.

7. WHAT THIS LICENSE DOES NOT RESTRICT

7.1  Rights that applicable law does not let a license take away. In
     Denmark these include a lawful user's right to make a backup copy,
     to observe, study and test the program, and to decompile it for
     interoperability (ophavsretsloven § 36, stk. 1, nr. 2 and 3, and
     § 37). Nothing in this license takes from a consumer any protection
     the law gives them.

7.2  Rights a hosting platform's terms require the Licensor, or whoever
     posts the Work there for it, to grant that platform's users, such
     as viewing and forking the Licensor's public repository on GitHub.
     Those rights stay as the platform defines them and are not extended
     by this license. Nothing in this license extends them to publishing
     a Human-Authored Derived Work.

7.3  The Licensor's rights in its names and marks. This license grants
     no right to use them. Keeping the Licensor's notices under
     Section 4.2(a), and copying this text under Section 12, are not
     such uses.

7.4  Text and data mining. The Licensor makes no reservation under
     ophavsretsloven § 11 b, stk. 2, or Article 4(3) of Directive (EU)
     2019/790.

8. ACCEPTANCE AND TERMINATION

8.1  The permissions in Section 3 and the rights in Section 7 need no
     acceptance. You accept this license by making or Distributing a
     Derived Work, by hand or through an Agent, by submitting content
     under Section 6, or in writing under Section 8.3. Acting only under
     a right in Section 7 is not acceptance.

8.2  If You breach this license, Your rights under Sections 4 and 5 end
     automatically. Sections 3 and 7 are not affected. Your rights are
     restored when You stop the breach and bring every copy You still
     make available into compliance with Section 4.2. Once the Licensor
     has notified You of the breach, You must do this within 30 days of
     the notice, and rights lost through a further breach after the
     notice are not restored under this Section. Restoration does not
     cover acts done while Your rights had ended. Obtaining another copy
     of the Work gives You no new rights while Yours have ended. Rights
     under this license end only as this Section states. Nothing in this
     Section affects a copy You lawfully acquired before Your rights
     ended: You may keep running it, correct its errors and pass it on
     as the law allows. If Your rights end, the rights of everyone who
     received the Work or an Agent-Authored Derived Work from You or
     through You, and who complies with this license, continue.

8.3  You accept in writing by stating, with Your name and the date,
     "[name] accepts the INGI Agent-Authored Derivatives License,
     version 0.3", in a Derived Work's notices, in a submission under
     Section 6, or in a message to the Licensor. It binds only the
     person it names. Copies need not carry it; Section 4.2(a) does not
     apply to it.

